# Byte-stable files: always LF in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
# src/shared/dossier.py::get_methodology_version_hash hashes METHODOLOGY.md with
# read_bytes(), so a CRLF checkout (Windows, core.autocrlf=true) gave a different
# methodology hash than Linux (defect D27). The claims seed and the method chapters
# are reproducibility inputs too. The committed blobs are already LF: this file
# changes only the Windows working copies, not the Linux hash.
METHODOLOGY.md text eol=lf
data/claims/*.jsonl text eol=lf
docs/method/** text eol=lf

# Never apply text conversion to images or PDFs, even under docs/method/.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
